<title>GERMANY: W.German Dec industry output rises 1.1 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>W.German Dec industry output rises 1.1 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT    Dec 96     Nov 96	 Dec 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   +1.1	 +1.1(+2.0)   -0.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +2.4	 +1.1(+2.1)    n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		96.8	 95.7(96.5)   94.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				     Dec 96		  Nov 96</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining		     91.4	 +6.3     86.0	 +2.1</p>
<p> Manufacturing output   95.7	 +0.5     95.2	 +1.4</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods  101.7	 +2.8     98.9	 +0.2</p>
<p>	Capital goods     92.8	 -3.1     95.8	 +3.0</p>
<p>	Consumer durables 82.1	 -1.3     83.2	 +2.3</p>
<p>	Consumer goods    92.9	 +1.5     91.5	 +1.1</p>
<p> Energy output	   109.1	 +1.4    107.6	 -0.6</p>
<p> Construction	    100.3	 +6.8     94.1	 -2.0</p>
<p>    Two month comparison Nov/Dec 96 with Sept/Oct 96:</p>
<p>    Industrial production	    +1.5</p>
<p>    Two month comparison Nov/Dec 96 with Nov/Dec 95:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +1.3</p>
<p> Mining				    -0.2</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		 +1.9</p>
<p>  Including:Intermediate goods     +3.9</p>
<p>		Capital goods	    +0.3</p>
<p>		Consumer durables	+1.9</p>
<p>		Consumer goods	   +0.3</p>
<p> Energy output			   +0.3</p>
<p> Construction			    -4.0</p>
<p>    -- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
